   This file MATERIALISES the license this software already declares — both
   `pyproject.toml` files in this repository carry
   `license = { text = "LicenseRef-Proprietary" }`, and until now no file
   delivered it. The license was NOT chosen here and no alternative was
   considered; that decision is not an engineering one.

   Counsel has not reviewed this text. Two facts in it were carried from the
   repository rather than settled, and each must be confirmed before sign-off:

     1. THE LEGAL ENTITY NAME. This file says "Integrum", which is what the
        SDK packaging descriptor declares (`authors = [{ name = "Integrum" }]`)
        and what the platform documentation uses. Internal drafting notes
        elsewhere in this repository instead use "Agentic OS, Inc." The two are
        not interchangeable in a legal instrument and only counsel can say
        which entity holds the copyright.

     2. THE COPYRIGHT YEARS. "2024-2026" is carried from the notice template in
        those same internal notes; it was not derived from first publication.

   Removing this block is part of sign-off, not part of tidying up.
